[h1]SaucedCarts v2.1.12[/h1]
[i]Released: 2026-06-17[/i]

[b]Carts can now spawn loaded with loot (opt-in BETA, off by default), updated for Build 42.19, plus fixes for dropping carts on stairs and a loot-respawn bug.[/b]

[h1]What's New[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Carts can now spawn with loot in them — opt-in BETA, off by default.[/b] Turn on the new "Loaded Cart Spawns [BETA]" sandbox option to let some carts spawn pre-loaded with gear that fits where they turn up: groceries by houses and in parking lots, food in grocery and convenience stores, building materials in warehouses and storage, tools in hardware and auto shops, and — very rarely — a survivor's stash of weapons and ammo. Rare / Some / Common control how often once it's enabled. It ships off by default while it gets more testing, the same way Corpse Storage shipped — so every cart stays empty unless you opt in.
[*][b]The cart push pose sticks properly during things like smoking and barricading.[/b] Doing one of those while holding a cart no longer leaves the cart stuck floating at your side.
[/list]

[h1]Bug Fixes[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Taking items straight from a container into your cart no longer stops that container from restocking.[/b] Previously, looting a shelf directly into a cart quietly switched off that container's loot respawn for good (the only fix was to drop an item in and take it back out). Looting into a cart now leaves the container able to restock normally.
[*][b]Dropping a cart while standing on stairs no longer sends it to the floor below.[/b] The cart now lands on a solid spot next to you instead of falling out of reach a level down.
[*][b]Carts no longer spawn inside parked cars or wedged where you can't reach them.[/b] Outdoor carts use the same parking spots the game uses for cars, so they occasionally landed inside a van or boxed in between gas-station pillars. They now only spawn somewhere you can actually walk up to.
[/list]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
[list]
[*]Updated for [b]Build 42.19[/b].
[*][b]Save-safe.[/b] No save-data changes — safe to upgrade mid-save. Existing carts and saves are unaffected.
[*][b]Addon authors:[/b] the cart-registration API is unchanged.
[/list]
